@model string
@*
    §1060(e)/(f) — the follow card. Operator 2026-08-11: *"make a button on the page where you give
    option to follow our linkedin company page if they dont follow it. mention it if your some
    precheck showed they either follow (say thank for following our page and mention they will be
    tagged) or tell them it is optional to be mentioned but they must opt-in to follow eldk linkedin
    company page"*.

    🔴 FIVE STATUSES, THREE MEANINGS, AND ONLY ONE OF THEM IS A CLAIM.
    `Participant.LinkedInPersonUrnStatus` is Resolved · NotAFollower · Ambiguous · KeywordUnusable ·
    LookupFailed. Only **Resolved** proves they follow (the mention endpoint resolves followers).
    **NotAFollower** is a real negative. The other three mean the lookup did not answer — and telling
    a real follower they do not follow us, because a sweep was throttled, is the exact failure
    §858.16h shaped that column to prevent. So everything that is not `Resolved` gets the same
    neutral INVITE, which is true whatever the unknown answer turns out to be.

    🔒 A PARTIAL, shared by the speaker and sponsor pages, so the wording cannot drift between them —
    the same reason SoMeAnnouncementQuery holds one scoping rule for both.
*@
@{
    var follows = string.Equals(Model, "Resolved", StringComparison.Ordinal);
    const string CompanyPage = "https://www.linkedin.com/company/experts-live-denmark/";
}

<div class="follow-card">
    @if (follows)
    {
        <p class="follow-line">
            <strong>You'll be tagged</strong> in posts about you — thanks for following our LinkedIn
            page.
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p class="follow-line">
            Being mentioned is <strong>optional</strong>. If you'd like us to tag you in posts about
            you, follow our LinkedIn company page — we can only tag people who follow it.
        </p>
        <a class="follow-btn" href="@CompanyPage" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Follow Experts Live Denmark
        </a>
    }
</div>

<style>
    /* Mobile-first (~360px): the button is full-width on a phone and shrinks to its text on a
       desktop, so it never becomes a full-width bar on a wide screen. */
    .follow-card {
        border: 1px solid #d0d4dd;
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 14px 16px;
        margin: 16px 0;
        background: #f6f8fc;
    }
    .follow-line { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; }
    .follow-card .follow-line:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .follow-btn {
        display: block;
        text-align: center;
        background: #0a66c2;            /* LinkedIn blue — this button goes to LinkedIn */
        color: #fff;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 700;
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 12px 20px;
        min-height: 44px;               /* a real tap target */
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }
    .follow-btn:hover, .follow-btn:focus { background: #004182; }
    @@media (min-width: 480px) {
        .follow-btn { display: inline-block; }
    }
</style>
